Once upon a time there was a girl who loved birthdays. I love birthdays

00:48:41.360 --> 00:48:49.200
She loved birthdays so much. She traveled all over the world to celebrate her friend's birthday

00:48:49.440 --> 00:48:55.760
She went to Iceland where they had special pancakes with syrup for her friend Bjorn's birthday

00:48:56.140 --> 00:49:00.000
Yeah, I love birthdays. She went to Nixon

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:03.900
where they had a piñata for her friend Carmen's birthday.

00:49:03.900 --> 00:49:06.700
A piñata is filled with goodies.

00:49:06.700 --> 00:49:12.940
Boy, a bowl of candy and a peso!

00:49:12.940 --> 00:49:15.740
I love birthdays!

00:49:15.740 --> 00:49:20.210
She went to Israel, where they played a game called Bli Yadahim

00:49:20.210 --> 00:49:22.210
for her friend Avi's birthday.

00:49:22.210 --> 00:49:25.810
Try to get your hat on your head without using your hands.

00:49:25.810 --> 00:49:30.000
Okay. I love these!

00:49:30.190 --> 00:49:35.470
When she got home to Ypsilanti, it was her birthday.

00:49:35.470 --> 00:49:38.110
Happy birthday!

00:49:38.110 --> 00:49:43.190
Oh yeah, I forgot. It's my birthday. I love birthdays.

00:49:43.190 --> 00:49:49.880
Coming up on the Birthday Channel: Born Free, Born on the Fourth of July, and Born Yesterday.

00:49:49.880 --> 00:49:52.120
Oh, thank you, TV.

00:49:52.120 --> 00:50:00.000
Wow, there's so many special things to do on birthdays, but Elmo wants to know more about birthdays.

00:50:00.280 --> 00:50:01.180
Don't you?

00:50:01.180 --> 00:50:03.000
How can we find out more?

00:50:07.660 --> 00:50:09.460
Want to talk to a birthday cake?

00:50:09.460 --> 00:50:12.660
Wow, yeah, we can talk to a birthday cake.

00:50:12.660 --> 00:50:14.220
Yay!

00:50:14.220 --> 00:50:16.360
Is it fun being a birthday cake?

00:50:16.360 --> 00:50:18.350
Yeah, it's a piece of cake.

00:50:18.350 --> 00:50:20.290
Ho, ho, ho, ho, ho.

00:50:20.290 --> 00:50:23.040
Tell Elmo more about birthdays, cake.

00:50:23.040 --> 00:50:28.010
Well, for starters, birthdays are to celebrate the day you were born.

00:50:28.010 --> 00:50:30.000
Oh, look!

00:50:31.150 --> 00:50:32.980
I'm imagining Elmo being born!

00:50:32.980 --> 00:50:37.430
Oh boy, George is almost a daddy!

00:50:37.430 --> 00:50:40.290
Boy, Gladys is almost a mommy!

00:50:40.290 --> 00:50:42.590
It's a boy!

00:50:47.820 --> 00:50:49.650
He is so cute!

00:50:49.650 --> 00:50:51.760
What are you going to name him?

00:50:51.760 --> 00:50:53.760
Elmo!

00:50:56.760 --> 00:51:00.000
And after that...

00:51:00.220 --> 00:51:02.960
You celebrate your birthday once a year.

00:51:02.960 --> 00:51:04.980
Some people like to have parties.

00:51:04.980 --> 00:51:07.200
Happy birthday, Elmo!

00:51:12.030 --> 00:51:17.540
When you get older, you can play games at your birthday parties.

00:51:17.540 --> 00:51:21.790
My favorite is Pin the Tail on the Donkey.

00:51:21.790 --> 00:51:23.970
Hey!

00:51:23.970 --> 00:51:25.730
I've already got a tail.

00:51:25.730 --> 00:51:26.970
See there?

00:51:26.970 --> 00:51:28.420
Oh, yeah!

00:51:28.420 --> 00:51:30.000
Sorry, Donkey!

00:51:30.030 --> 00:51:39.760
And you always sing the birthday song to celebrate the day you were born.

00:51:39.760 --> 00:51:40.870
Yeah!

00:51:40.870 --> 00:51:44.430
So let's sing the birthday song to Dorothy.

00:51:44.430 --> 00:51:45.430
Be right back.

00:51:45.430 --> 00:51:46.390
Good idea.

00:51:46.390 --> 00:51:50.610
I love singing the birthday song.

00:51:50.610 --> 00:51:51.780
Ta-da!

00:51:51.780 --> 00:51:52.780
Oh, nice hat.

00:51:52.780 --> 00:51:53.780
Oh, thank you.

00:51:53.780 --> 00:51:54.780
You're welcome.

00:51:54.780 --> 00:51:55.780
Here we go.

00:51:55.780 --> 00:51:57.400
Oh, you can sing along too.

00:51:57.400 --> 00:52:00.000
This is for you, Dorothy.

00:52:15.840 --> 00:52:18.540
by the letter R.

00:52:18.540 --> 00:52:20.870
Got today's letter, sink.

00:52:31.470 --> 00:52:32.790
But what's today's number?

00:52:34.890 --> 00:52:35.870
There it is.

00:52:36.190 --> 00:52:37.260
What number is it?

00:52:37.360 --> 00:52:37.880
17.

00:52:38.220 --> 00:52:40.930
Yes, 17 is the number of the day.

00:52:41.190 --> 00:52:47.140
So, Sesame Street was brought to you today by the letter B, by the number 17.

00:52:48.160 --> 00:52:51.140
This is Murray saying, see you next time on the street.

00:52:51.720 --> 00:52:52.220
Peace.
